virals.text:
the problem with vibe-coding internal tools: one person builds it in Codex, another in Claude Code, and nothing travels between them. no shared data, no access control, no way for the rest of the team to use it.

@deepnotehq just launched data apps. describe what you want, the agent builds the interface and the notebook behind it. connected to 120+ data sources. every version saved. share by link.

the difference: most AI artifacts are static and get rebuilt from scratch. a Deepnote data app runs on a live notebook, so the data stays current. and your whole team can use it without opening a notebook.

works across Codex and Claude Code. run locally or publish to Deepnote.

@jakubjurovych

